# Cloudflare Workers static-assets headers for damiao-motor.jia-xie.com.
#
# This site is served by an assets-only Worker (no Worker script), so a
# _headers file applies here — unlike jia-xie.com, where the entry Worker means
# headers have to be set in code instead. Keep it that way.
#
# TWO RULES OF THIS FILE:
#
# 1. Rules that set the same header MUST NOT overlap. Cloudflare concatenates
#    them rather than picking the most specific, so /assets/* plus /*.jpg gave
#    `Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, public, max-age=31536000, immutable`
#    on one response. The /* block below is safe to overlap only because it sets
#    no Cache-Control.
#
# 2. `immutable` is only for content-addressed filenames. Not everything under
#    /assets/ is hashed — Material hashes its own bundles (main.<hash>.min.css,
#    bundle.<hash>.min.js) but extra.css, _mkdocstrings.css, favicon.png and the
#    lunr.*.min.js search files keep stable names. Freezing those for a year
#    would mean a palette edit never reaching anyone who had already visited.
#    Anything not hashed gets a week at most; the default (revalidate every
#    time) is the right answer for HTML.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=300

# Hashed by MkDocs Material — the filename changes when the content does.
/assets/stylesheets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Mixed: bundle.<hash>.min.js is hashed, the lunr.*.min.js search files are not.
# A week suits both.
/assets/javascripts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/assets/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/assets/og-card.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

# Deliberately not listed, so they keep the revalidating default:
#   /assets/extra.css, /assets/_mkdocstrings.css  — stable names, edited by hand
#   every *.html                                  — doc edits must go live at once
